<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-01-handwashing" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Handwashing</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      We begin our exploration into the fascinating chemistry happening in our home by looking at how we wash our hands.
      The familiar products we use <mdash/> soap and rubbing alcohol <mdash/> work so much better than pure water. Why is that?
    </p>

    <p>
      The core theme in this chapter will be <term>polarity</term>, as we will see that it governs many of the molecular interactions we will discuss in this chapter.
      <idx><h>polarity</h></idx>
    </p>
  </introduction>
